WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.600
If you know about Montreal you've probably heard about a few things.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.640
It's known for its European architecture and cobblestone streets.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:17.460
It's the origin of the world-famous Cirque de Soleil. And it's home to the best poutine in the world

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.780
But it's also known for its nightlife.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.540
"Now wait a minute now, are strippers paid hourly here? Is that right?"

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.120
"It's not a tip system?"

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.420
"Uh yeah it's considered an art — a performance art."

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.200
And esports fans associate Montreal with one thing: controversy.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.400
Montreal is the only Canadian city where DreamHack runs tournaments

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.060
and one particular tournament was the beginning of the end for

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:53.680
Immortals' former CS:GO roster. DreamHack Montreal 2017 was a pretty unimportant tournament despite

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:59.840
Its $100,000 prize pool. It was just too soon after the Krakow Major to draw any notable teams.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.660
Krakow was the first Major that Immortals qualified for after a string of failures

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.460
(Casting)

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:33.200
(Casting)

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.680
They perpetually played little brother to their Brazilian countrymen in Luminosity Gaming and later, SK Gaming.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.280
Partially because of their age but also because of their worse results.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.540
At Krakow, their inexperience shown in the groups.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.700
But they were in their element come playoffs. They fed off the energy of the crowd and achieved a breakthrough

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.220
performance.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:02:28.780
(Casting)

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.240
After that event, they were no longer the team that failed to make the majors again

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.380
and again. They were no longer SK's little brothers

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.320
There were a team that demanded respect.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.300
In the offseason, multiple reports came out that  IMT were going through internal issues

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.180
and might face roster changes.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.600
Immortals’ roster remained unchanged.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.220
But they headed into their first event post-Krakow,

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.840
DreamHack Masters Malmo with a cloud hanging over their heads.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.020
They had a decent showing in Malmo and advanced to the playoffs over Fnatic.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.160
But fell to North after a tight quarterfinal.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.160
(Casting)

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.740
It was a disappointing finish the Major grand finalists,

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.240
but some fans brushed it off as growing pains for a young  roster.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.220
But there were plenty of questions for Immortals heading into DreamHack Montreal.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.880
Aside from North, Montreal featured a lower tier of competition than the Major.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.160
A majority of the teams were from the Americas

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.720
so expectations were high for Immortals.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.620
And they didn't disappoint.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:51.980
(Casting)

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.660
Immortals earned a spot in the Grand Finals against North,

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.060
the team that eliminated them from Malmo just a week prior.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.960
So Immortals went into the series with a chip on their shoulders.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.780
Well... Two of them did.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.240
Boltz and steel showed up on time,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.960
but the rest of the team didn't.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.000
"But what we are waiting on is the Immortals who are well, they're not quite seated just yet

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:21.500
but any moment hopefully, it will be Immortals freshened up and sitting down after that performance earlier that

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.680
landed them here."

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.440
In fact, they took so long to arrive at the venue that

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.300
Immortals were handed a default map loss.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.680
"Well guess what guys I have an easter egg for you.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:36.360
And it is that we will not be seeing the first map of Mirage, it does

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:40.080
look like the Immortals have forfeited it. Due to being late.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.280
To the stage and to playing and that's just, the way the cookie crumbled I suppose.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.760
I don't really know what else to say about that other than the process needs to be respected.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.580
And rules by tournament organizers need to be respected.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:56.360
And the right thing, is certainly I believe right here."

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.800
With the Brazilian side already down a map,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.380
team morale was undoubtedly low.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.100
And the rest of the series went about the way you'd expect.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.940
"Yeah well, if North wanted to win before they sure are now."

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.280
"It's over."

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:22.720
(Casting)

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:27.180
Some time during the series then-CLG coach Steve "Ryu" Rattacasa

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.460
tweeted that the team had been late for their series earlier that day,

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.860
and that he had heard that some of the players had been out the night before partying.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.200
Fifteen minutes after that, CLG player FNS tweeted that

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.320
he was disappointed to have been eliminated by hungover players.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.860
It didn’t take long for the Immortals players to notice.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.860
FNS and LUCAS1 had a back and forth, that ended relatively peacefully.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.680
But kNg’s response was less reserved.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.340
And it didn't end there.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.800
According to FNS, he was told to leave the hotel he was staying at

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:02.900
because kNg was going through the halls looking for him.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:08.040
"I was in our hotel room whatever chilling, and then I'm like, "I'm hungry as sh*t let's go to Moxie's or something."

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.020
And I go downstairs and,

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.840
A person that I'm not going to name, walks up to me  and says, "Hey man like

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.080
you really really just like, you gotta go.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.900
You gotta go. You really just gotta leave."

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.180
And I'm like, "What's going on?"

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:28.480
He's like, "Dude. Like you tweeted this, and I understand that it was a joke, but kNg like

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.760
is not happy with you right now and he's looking for you."

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.540
And I'm like, "I don't know what to say to that."

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.960
Can we just pause for a second and talk about how insane this is?

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:42.120
Here’s FNS, a guy from Canada who makes a living playing video games,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.860
what more could you ask for?

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.040
He just lost a set and was feeling cheeky,

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.000
so he spat out a tweet that was edgy and self-deprecating

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.560
and as he was getting ready to head out, someone stopped him and told him he had to leave the hotel

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.340
because there was somebody stalking the hall looking for him.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.380
This was no longer just a joke for FNS.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:03.540
"All the other information I got is I need to leave, this guy's temper is out of control,

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.560
I gotta go.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:08.300
And I'm like... So in my head I'm thinking like why is he looking for me.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.960
Because the way normally. The way people have confronted me usually is like

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:15.600
they message me or they come up to me say, "Hey what you did was messed up."

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.720
It's understandable for things to get heated in a competitive space.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.100
And it's easy to brush things like this off.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.420
Especially when the medium is as distant and impotent as a tweet.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.380
But a death threat, no matter where it comes from, should never be taken lightly.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:32.280
"I've been thinking about killing you in real life lately." That's not nice homie.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:42.020
Jesus all I do is play video games man. Actually, I'm gonna report that guy to the police.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.460
I'm also gonna report this to Twitch, get his info.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.580
"I love you calm down bro I was kidding, chat was boring had to get it lit."

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.540
"I've donated 1K check your PayPal donations damn I feel bad now."

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.280
What the f*** dude that's not something you joke about man.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.240
And I only saw one donation from you and it was that one.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.940
Don't threaten someone's life bro like joke or not it's ridiculous."

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.300
Despite all the commotion and hearsay,

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:16.480
no one ever actually provided proof that kNg was stalking the halls looking for FNS.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.920
But it kind of didn't matter.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:20.920
If you put aside everything that was “he said, she said,”

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:24.120
regardless of whether the source was trustworthy or reputable.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.700
the facts remain.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.440
Immortals were late for a Grand Final.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:32.340
Something unheard of in top tier competition, esports or otherwise.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.280
And kNg went on to make a very public death threat on Twitter.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:40.340
All eyes were on those moments. There was nothing to prove.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.080
So yeah, things were bad.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:45.080
Should Immortals have been late for their match? No.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:47.980
Should FNS have made that joke? Probably not.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.900
Should kNg have made those death threats? Absolutely not.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.180
But the aftermath had even more of a lasting effect.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.020
Several of the Immortals players apologized for the lackluster Grand Finals,

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.680
regardless of how it happened.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.400
Including kNg.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.880
But two months after the incident, there still wasn’t any closure between FNS and kNg.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.980
"No there's not been any contact with kNg, as far as like any of that stuff.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.200
I'm pretty sure he still hates me, but as far as like everybody else I think I'm chill with the team.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:20.840
When it happened, I was ready to talk to him but he was like kind of upset. Obviously.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.580
And so he didn't want to have any conversations with me.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.180
Or rather his coach just told me just not to bother.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:31.320
But yeah I did try at first but now it's like kind of, water under the bridge."

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.880
And even if he did apologize,

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.740
it would do little to erase his threat from the public record.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:40.240
Thanks in part to the CS:GO community, who immediately turned it into a meme.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.000
"We should not push kNg he seems to be sober."

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.660
"Let's do pistol armor."

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.460
But the death threat itself

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:52.740
had a lasting negative impact on kNg's career.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.380
"But he also needs to chill. Like he's applying for a Visa right now.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:01.940
If they google his name, if they look at any  of the stuff, it's not good for him."

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:05.400
"You know what I mean? Like he needs to — he should be in damage control mode."

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.060
kNg was put on the chopping block,

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:11.460
but his four teammates and coach convinced Immortals’ CEO Noah Whinston to let him stay.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.200
But then he violated his internal suspension

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.620
and his contract was immediately terminated.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:19.820
"And is not a part of Immortals and will never again be a part of Immortals."

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.400
Noah ran the risk of pissing off his players for the sake of principle.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.320
And that’s exactly what happened.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:29.660
The Teles twins quickly requested a transfer once they heard the news that kNg was gone.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.720
But it was a decision that was almost universally praised by the esports community.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:39.420
"Ultimately though I don't want this to be the conclusion of this sordid saga.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:45.080
I was not left with many options if we wanted to preserve the philosophies and the ideals

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.060
that Immortals as a brand stands for.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:51.220
Though it is unfortunate that Valve rules means that the three players no longer with us,

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:53.380
have control over our Major slot,

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:58.980
playing in a Major is not worth more than everything that we stand for as an organization."

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:04.420
Later, the ex-Immortals trio (and the Major spot that they held) were bought by 100 Thieves.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:08.220
"We're permanently moving into the CS:GO community, and we are teaming up with

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.920
kNg, LUCAS, HEN1, fnx, and Bit."

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.980
However, 100 Thieves' players, perhaps unsurprisingly,

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.280
Couldn't secure visas in time, and weren't able to attend the Major.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.180
The team never played a single match.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:25.880
"Maybe it's karma, maybe it's justice for them that the 100 Theives guys didn't make it.

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:32.200
And I'm not gonna lie I'm kinda conflicted. Like I kind of feel like you good, serves you right. But at the same

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:36.520
time you know you don't want to see that happen to a team that's trying to make a living and get to a Major."

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:41.300
It's hard to say exactly how much of a part Montreal played in kNg's downfall.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.620
But it's obvious that Montreal is where that downfall began.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:49.420
A handful of tweets, four months and however many alleged encounters behind the scenes,

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:53.660
were all it took to destroy the career of a truly promising player.

